      given: "Exports were gum, groundnuts and palm oil; by the mid-19th century palm oil was West Africa's major export item; European merchants controlled export and internal trade.",
      formula: "Historical concept: an economic change must be judged by who gains and who loses, not only by what is traded.",
      substitution: "Profits went to most African rulers and wealthy merchants, while imported cloth weakened local crafts and firearms helped rulers plunder their own people.",
