      given: "Britain led abolition after the Industrial Revolution; the new 'Legitimate Trade' grew; European commercial competition increased in the 1870s and 1880s.",
      formula: "Historical concept: economic change can drive political expansion as nations seek raw materials and markets.",
      substitution: "European industries needed raw materials and markets, so competition for West African trade grew.",
      calculation: "That commercial rivalry culminated in the Scramble for Africa in the 1870s and 1880s and the Berlin Conference.",
